note E14 bound rule (positive): the secret byte goes to c[40 + (i & 63)], offsets 40..103 of a 104-byte layout,
note outside the declared count field [32,40). AND-mask range plus constant 40 gives [40,103]. With e14 the
note store is excused (bounded-offset); without e14 its address is unknown.
fn f c edit uchar 104 a view uchar 1 i ulong to ulong
put c add 40 and i 63 get a 0
if eq get c 32 0
ret 0
end
ret 1
end
